From 94c80762cb7d0c66b7e3b57a806351f5d0a68b12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abinash Haldorai <abinash.haldorai@eka.care>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:00:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Integrations: add the telephony channel with a Vobiz
 provider

A phone number patients dial can now be registered as an integration
(channel "telephony", provider "vobiz") and bound to an agent through the
existing product-binding API, the same way a WhatsApp number is.

- integration/schemas/telephone: Vobiz credentials. The dialled number
  (E.164, normalised) is the account identity; an optional public_number
  records the clinic's own number when it forwards. No secrets are stored.
- The channel was already declared but had no schema; register it so the
  number is validated and uniquely keyed per workspace.
- Add "vobiz" to the provider choices (migration 0004, no database change).
- webhooks.inbound_url: a telephony number's URL is matrix's voice answer
  route by integration uuid (MATRIX_VOICE_BASE_URL), not doot's.
- Detail page tells the user to set it as the Vobiz Answer URL.

Matrix has no route for this URL yet; that is the next change. Not tested
against a database or a real Vobiz account (migration generated with
makemigrations; integration tests run without a database).

